{"agent":"impl-sw-launch","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"`launch()` starts the lane at `drv.start(prep.spec)` before writing the required audit note. If `_audit` (or the preceding `json.dumps`) fails after the start, the exception propagates and the caller receives neither `Launched` nor `Refused`, while the lane is already running. For example, if `req.log` is an event log on a read-only audit volume, `req.log.append(...)` at line 185 can raise `PermissionError` after `drv.start` succeeds; the scheduler then cannot track or stop the lane and may retry, launching another lane and exceeding `max_lanes` or the budget. This violates the documented postcondition that a failure/refusal starts nothing and that a successful launch produces the audit note.","digest":"5420c9f348023416","location":"ddflow/services/lanes/launch.py:171-186","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/lanes/launch.py:171-186"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"`load` assumes the TOML value under `template` is a mapping. If a launch-template file contains valid TOML such as `template = \"x\"` or an array of tables `[[template]]`, the expression `doc.get(\"template\", {}).items()` raises `AttributeError` instead of returning `(templates, notes)` as documented. For example, a configured file containing only `template = \"x\"` makes the scheduler tick crash when loading templates rather than receiving a note that the file is malformed.","digest":"6408ada6dcd5b808","location":"ddflow/services/lanes/launch_template.py:load","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/lanes/launch_template.py:load"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"`load` catches `OSError` and `tomllib.TOMLDecodeError`, but not `UnicodeDecodeError` from `path.read_text(\"utf-8\")`. If the configured template file contains invalid UTF-8 bytes (for example, a file whose content is `b\"\\xff\"`), `load` raises `UnicodeDecodeError` instead of returning the promised “cannot be read” note. This can crash the scheduler tick when a corrupt or non-UTF-8 template file is present.","digest":"99fe668284e92fc6","location":"ddflow/services/lanes/launch_template.py:load","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/lanes/launch_template.py:load"},{"chunk":5,"detail":"The autouse `_env` fixture clears Git variables and sets `LAN_ENDPOINT_KEY`, but it never removes `DDFLOW_AGENT`. The fake harness records `os.environ.get(\"DDFLOW_AGENT\")`, and `test_approved_template_starts_a_lane_with_the_seed_pack_and_audits` asserts `seen[\"agent\"] == \"lane-7\"` to prove that launch passes the lane agent into the child process. If the test process already has `DDFLOW_AGENT=lane-7` in its environment, that assertion can pass even when `LN.launch` does not set `DDFLOW_AGENT` at all, because the child inherits the variable. The fixture should delete `DDFLOW_AGENT` (e.g. `monkeypatch.delenv(\"DDFLOW_AGENT\", raising=False)`) to make the test actually verify the launched environment.","digest":"8f00ebf9a9b87da8","location":"tests/test_lane_launch.py:_env","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_lane_launch.py:_env"}],"chunks_total":5,"coverage":"5/5 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":30562,"diff_sha":"0037fffdc01cfdfb1b94541e108c9d1fc776934f3c9b53165eeb32719ffbe59d","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":773.2,"excluded_bytes":4338,"excluded_files":2,"excluded_paths":["README.md","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_outputs.ambr"],"family":"alibaba","findings":4,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","output_digest":"84a539b67ce78a04","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/SW-launch.rubber_duck.qwen3.8-flash-next-fp8.20261031T142256Z-b3ea1cfe.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4,5],"reviewed_head":"7242ae2fa91fe92ae179ce9a2255ae175ae3ecbc","reviewed_paths":{"README.md":"100644 ea9d332c0a5656ae701646126f99aa7cdf0e001