{"agent":"impl-sw-launch","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"In `_constraints`, the `cost is None` branch refuses a launch whenever `req.est_in` or `req.est_out` is nonzero, without checking `[REDACTED:host]`. Given a local template (`[REDACTED:host]=True`) with no verified price (so `score.est_cost(...)` returns `None`) and nonzero token estimates, the function returns `Refused((\"cost cannot be estimated: the template has no verified price\",))`, even though the next branch explicitly exempts local lanes from the budget check (`elif cost > t.budget_usd and not [REDACTED:host]`). This blocks local lanes that legitimately have no monetary price.","digest":"bf45fd9094d7ca05","location":"ddflow/services/lanes/launch.py:_constraints","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/lanes/launch.py:_constraints"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"`load` assumes `doc.get(\"template\", {})` is a mapping and immediately calls `.items()`. A syntactically valid TOML file such as `template = []` (or `template = \"x\"`, `template = 1`, etc.) makes `doc[\"template\"]` a list/string/int, so line 157 raises `AttributeError` instead of returning the documented “cannot be read” note. A scheduler tick that calls `load` on an edited template file can therefore crash on malformed-but-valid TOML.","digest":"8cb40548b1c26332","location":"ddflow/services/lanes/launch_template.py:157","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/lanes/launch_template.py:157"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"`load` catches `OSError` and `tomllib.TOMLDecodeError`, but `path.read_text(\"utf-8\")` can raise `UnicodeDecodeError` (a `ValueError`, not caught here) when the template file is not valid UTF-8. For example, a template file containing byte `0xFF` causes line 152 to propagate `UnicodeDecodeError` instead of returning `{path.name}: cannot be read: ...` as intended.","digest":"429a765fa6e6300b","location":"ddflow/services/lanes/launch_template.py:152","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/lanes/launch_template.py:152"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"`problems` rejects negative `trust` and `budget_usd`, but it does not reject negative `price_in` or `price_out`, even though those fields are documented as “USD per million tokens, for the budget check.” A template with `price_in = -1.0`, `price_out = -1.0`, `budget_usd = 1.0`, `local = false`, `harness = \"opencode\"`, `route = \"r\"`, and `family = \"f\"` passes `_row`/`problems`. If launch uses these documented price fields to estimate cost, the estimate can be negative and therefore always “below” the budget, defeating the per-template budget refusal.","digest":"6f1cf2fa544f3727","location":"ddflow/services/lanes/launch_template.py:82","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/lanes/launch_template.py:82"}],"chunks_total":6,"coverage":"6/6 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":33462,"diff_sha":"31219b0b65292b52d6edebad9c5ada77559a6219d0aec69953ab383e34fc707a","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":999.0,"excluded_bytes":4338,"excluded_files":2,"excluded_paths":["README.md","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_outputs.ambr"],"family":"alibaba","findings":4,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","output_digest":"35b62e0538f733dc","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/SW-launch.rubber_duck.qwen3.8-flash-next-fp8.20261031T142228Z-34e05fa9.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4,5,6],"reviewed_head":"c2b83390ac17834fa8896e44d884e7280cbf1593","reviewed_paths":{"README.md":"100644 ea9d332c0a5656ae701646126f99aa7cdf0e0019","ddflow/config_sections/swarm.py":"100644 da420d312407e69e6fc5beeafb6522604811817c","ddflow/services/lanes/launch.py":"100644 75cafb0dbe4788d54689ad9c456e3a6c1c0bf042","ddflow/services/lanes/launch_template.py":"100644 a721bf5499cce360149039bd0f216218ce96fdda","ddflow/templates/upgrade/unreleased/knob_added.