{"agent":"impl-sw-launch","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"When `OC.prepare` returns `LH.Consent` because the lane’s hook plugin still needs a person’s approval, `launch` immediately calls `OC.cleanup(req.home)` before returning the consent. The module docstring says the plugin’s consent is “asked there” in the private home; deleting that home destroys the pending consent/inspection context. For a template whose hook plugin has not yet been consented, the caller receives a `Refused.consent` whose `how` may point to a now-deleted home, so the operator cannot actually grant the consent and every subsequent launch repeats the same refusal.","digest":"7405bb63bc5752c2","location":"ddflow/services/lanes/launch.py:160-162","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/lanes/launch.py:160-162"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"`problems` rejects negative `trust` and `budget_usd`, but it never checks `price_in` or `price_out`. A template file such as `[template.foo] harness = \"opencode\" route = \"r\" family = \"f\" budget_usd = 1.0 price_in = -1000000.0 price_out = 0.0` passes `_bad_type` and `problems`, so `load` returns it and `consent` can be approved. Since those fields are documented as USD per million tokens for the budget check, a negative price makes the estimated launch cost negative (or zero if clamped), so a lane with actual positive token usage is not “above” the budget and can bypass the budget refusal.","digest":"b8d1b66bdc85533e","location":"ddflow/services/lanes/launch_template.py:82","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/lanes/launch_template.py:82"}],"chunks_total":5,"coverage":"5/5 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":31642,"diff_sha":"c0dc606b0750a4f581bcd7d2200c8b20cddb4fecf0497aa4d05f72f0614126ed","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":1372.3,"excluded_bytes":4338,"excluded_files":2,"excluded_paths":["README.md","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_outputs.ambr"],"family":"alibaba","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","output_digest":"e381a10da36e3e1f","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/SW-launch.critic.qwen3.8-flash-next-fp8.20261031T145652Z-9d4b83d6.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4,5],"reviewed_head":"86ee851ede18e4497e690b5c83cf04b602303a0a","reviewed_paths":{"README.md":"100644 ea9d332c0a5656ae701646126f99aa7cdf0e0019","ddflow/config_sections/swarm.py":"100644 da420d312407e69e6fc5beeafb6522604811817c","ddflow/services/lanes/launch.py":"100644 6b2203d258ae041883d4bede052eb801ba4ceeca","ddflow/services/lanes/launch_template.py":"100644 76d1b8c1da646d4d62abefcee8be8640382888ad","ddflow/templates/upgrade/unreleased/knob_added.swarm.launch_enabled.toml":"100644 f3d06951b5d1d3b7310bb087d20c3f08ffe08a25","ddflow/templates/upgrade/unreleased/knob_added.swarm.launch_max_budget_usd.toml":"100644 d94f277c4d06b9cb465c86e07c913af2692bbec3","ddflow/templates/upgrade/unreleased/knob_added.swarm.launch_templates_file.toml":"100644 f61c932dddae91535b8aabc82dde0e0fc20980b6","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_outputs.ambr":"100644 5fcd4f89a6b1889452f9afad732a47c60ed294fe","tests/test_lane_launch.py":"100644 ff54f607a47bb86c835158d780dc548cce501561"},"reviewer":"qwen3.8-flash-next-fp8","reviewer_digest":"3926c0df5644d7de","round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/services/lanes/launch.py:160-162","ddflow/services/lanes/launch_template.py:82"],"tree_sha":"5324fab8a0aa+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":2},"gate":"critic","reason":"2 finding(s)"},"id":"ecfc0e03ec2537a6e750b9b3d","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":119298,"schema":1,"subject":"SW-launch","ts":"2026-10-31T15:59:04.326499Z"}
